{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-spawn-vessel-004-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/IdentityLossClassifierTests.cs", "line": 379, "method": "ActiveRootBackgrounded_FlushForwardsControllers_AllowingIdentityLossOverride", "category": "T1", "severity": "High", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/FlightRecorder.cs:6983; stub the AdoptControllersIfEmpty backstop -> still green (the test performs the forward itself)", "what_it_asserts": "that AdoptControllersIfEmpty populates a null-Controllers tree root and that the pure identity-loss predicate then returns true", "why_weak": "the production backstop it names (FlightRecorder StartRecording forwarding pendingStartControllers to the active tree recording) is replaced by an inline call in the test; grep shows no other test file touches pendingStartControllers, so removing that backstop reds nothing while the identity-loss override silently stops firing for the active-root-backgrounded shape", "proposed_action": "drive the forward through FlightRecorder (or expose a seam for the backstop block) and assert the tree root gained Controllers without the test calling AdoptControllersIfEmpty", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-spawn-vessel-004-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/IdentityLossClassifierTests.cs", "line": 731, "method": "RetiredEntry_DoesNotTriggerBackgroundStateDrift", "category": "T1", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/BackgroundRecorder.cs RetireDestroyedBackgroundEntry; stub the retirement drain -> still green (the test hand-builds the post-retirement state)", "what_it_asserts": "that the drift warner logs no drift line naming a retired pid", "why_weak": "the retired pid is never inserted into BackgroundMap by the test and the warner only iterates BackgroundMap, so the assertion is true by construction; the retirement path itself is never invoked", "proposed_action": "call the retirement path on a recording that IS in BackgroundMap and assert the entry was removed and the warner stays quiet afterwards", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "coverage", "sut": "FlightRecorder", "sut_file": "Source/Parsek/FlightRecorder.cs", "sut_line": 6983, "case_kind": "integration", "proposed_name": "StartRecording_ActiveTreeRootMissingControllers_ForwardsPendingStartControllers", "sketch": "arrange an ActiveTree whose ActiveRecordingId points at a Recording with Controllers==null; run the recorder path that populates pendingStartControllers and reaches the backstop block; assert the tree root's Controllers now carry the captured pids and the Verbose 'forwarded N controller part(s)' line was written", "guards": "a regression that drops the tree-root controller forwarding, which silently disables the BG identity-loss override for backgrounded active roots", "risk": "recording"}
